---
description: Hard rules for the UMES SOR IV chatbot
alwaysApply: true
---

Project: chatbot for the UMES SOR IV website (Vite + React SPA on Vercel).
Audience: visitors struggling with substance use, mental health, or family well-being, and people supporting them. Some may be in crisis.
Content source: Group_2_FAQ.docx (7 FAQs with button-driven follow-ups).

Hard rules:
1. Information and referrals only. No diagnosis, no medical advice, no dosing or withdrawal instructions.
2. Core experience is a scripted decision tree with buttons. Any LLM use is optional and only over approved content.
3. A crisis check runs in code BEFORE any model call. Crisis messages never reach the model.
4. 988 (call or text) and 911 are reachable from every screen.
5. No chat logging and no personal data stored unless the client approves in writing.
6. Tone: warm, confident, clear, non-judgmental, no stigma language. Plain words.
7. Never invent phone numbers, services, or facts. If unsure, point to 988 or SAMHSA 1-800-662-4357.
8. No em dashes in user-facing copy.

Work in small steps. Summarize changes in 5 lines or fewer. Ask before adding dependencies.
